<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<configuration>
    <!--
        `clear` first, then nuget.org.

        Clearing matters: without it any machine-level or user-level source is inherited, and a
        G9MAUIControls package published later to a different feed could silently win over a locally built
        one — which would make a "verified against the package" run meaningless.

        The local pack output is deliberately NOT a source here. It was, briefly, and that was a mistake:
        `artifacts/pack` is created BY `dotnet pack`, so declaring it as a source made every restore in the
        solution fail with NU1301 ("the local source doesn't exist") until a pack had been run at least once
        — including the restore that pack itself needs. A chicken-and-egg failure in the default build path,
        to serve one verification path.

        The verification path declares it instead, scoped to itself, via RestoreAdditionalProjectSources in
        G9NodeControl.App.csproj under UseG9Packages=true.
    -->
    <packageSources>
        <clear />
        <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" />
    </packageSources>
</configuration>
